###############################################################################
# E-commerce Order Management — runnable walkthrough
#
# Works in IntelliJ HTTP Client and the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Start the app first:  mvn spring-boot:run
#
# Run the requests top to bottom. Tokens and ids are captured automatically,
# so nothing needs pasting by hand.
#
# Scenario A  happy path: browse -> cart -> preview -> checkout -> fulfil -> return -> refund
# Scenario B  idempotency: the same key twice
# Scenario C  payment failures: declined, and unknown-outcome with self-healing
# Scenario D  oversell: a SKU with exactly one unit
# Scenario E  admin: catalog, stock, coupons, operations
###############################################################################

@host = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

###############################################################################
# SCENARIO A — the happy path
###############################################################################

### A1. Log in as a customer
# @name customerLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "customer@oms.dev", "password": "Password@123" }

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.data.accessToken); %}

### A2. Who am I?
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A3. Browse the Audio category — no token needed
GET {{api}}/products?categorySlug=audio&size=5

### A4. Product detail. `variants[].id` is what the cart expects.
GET {{api}}/products/3

### A5. Add 2 x Nimbus Buds Pro (variant 4, 7999.00 each)
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 4, "quantity": 2 }

### A6. Read the cart
# Note the cart holds no prices and reserves no stock: check A7 for real numbers,
# and note availability in E4 is unchanged by having items in a basket.
GET {{api}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A7. Preview with a coupon — the interesting call
#
#   subtotal  15998.00   2 x 7999.00
#   discount    500.00   SAVE10 is 10% (1599.80) but CAPS at 500.00
#   tax        2789.64   18% of 15498.00 — the POST-discount base
#   shipping      0.00   free above 999.00 post-discount
#   total     18287.64
#
# Also note lines[0].lineDiscount: the coupon apportioned down to the line,
# which is what makes a correct partial refund computable later (A15).
POST {{api}}/cart/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "couponCode": "SAVE10", "destinationZone": "WEST" }

### A8. Place the order. `Idempotency-Key` is required.
# The response total is EXACTLY the previewed total — both run one pricing engine.
# @name checkout
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-happy-path-0001

{
  "shippingAddress": {
    "recipientName": "Cara Customer",
    "line1": "42 Marine Drive, Flat 9B",
    "city": "Mumbai",
    "zone": "WEST",
    "postalCode": "400020",
    "phone": "9000000002"
  },
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentToken": "tok_success",
  "couponCode": "SAVE10"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("orderId", response.body.data.orderId);
  client.global.set("orderNumber", response.body.data.orderNumber);
%}

### A9. The async pipeline already ran — after the response was returned
GET {{api}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A10. The order, with money breakdown and `allowedNextStatuses`
GET {{api}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### A11. Log in as Mumbai warehouse staff
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "staff.mum@oms.dev", "password": "Password@123" }

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.data.accessToken); %}

### A12. The work queue — these shipments were created asynchronously
GET {{api}}/fulfillment/queue?status=PENDING
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A13. Find this order's parcel
# @name shipments
GET {{api}}/fulfillment/orders/{{orderId}}/shipments
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

> {% client.global.set("shipmentId", response.body.data[0].id); %}

### A14a. Pack it — the order follows to PACKED
POST {{api}}/fulfillment/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "PACKED" }

### A14b. Ship it — a tracking number is minted here
POST {{api}}/fulfillment/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "SHIPPED" }

### A14c. Deliver it — starts the return window
POST {{api}}/fulfillment/shipments/{{shipmentId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "DELIVERED" }

### A14d. Cancelling now is refused: the goods are with a carrier
# Expect 409 ILLEGAL_TRANSITION, naming DELIVERED as the allowed move.
POST {{api}}/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "too late" }

### A15. Grab the order line id, then request a PARTIAL return (1 of 2)
# @name orderForReturn
GET {{api}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

> {% client.global.set("orderLineId", response.body.data.lines[0].orderLineId); %}

### A16. Request the return
# totalRefund is 9143.82 — half of the 18287.64 actually PAID, with the discount
# share and tax both reversed. Half the list price would be 7999.00.
# Nothing is refunded or restocked yet.
# @name returnRequest
POST {{api}}/orders/{{orderId}}/returns
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "SIZE_MISMATCH",
  "comment": "Ordered medium, needed large",
  "lines": [ { "orderLineId": {{orderLineId}}, "quantity": 1 } ]
}

> {% client.global.set("returnId", response.body.data.id); %}

### A17. Staff review queue
GET {{api}}/returns/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A18. Approve: refund, then restock to the warehouse that shipped it
# The order returns to DELIVERED (not RETURNED) because one unit is still out,
# and payment becomes PARTIALLY_REFUNDED.
POST {{api}}/returns/{{returnId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "Goods received in original packaging" }

### A19. Confirm: refundedTotal set, returnedQuantity 1, returnableQuantity 1
GET {{api}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

###############################################################################
# SCENARIO B — idempotency
###############################################################################

### B1. Add an item
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 4, "quantity": 1 }

### B2. Check out with a fixed key
# @name idemFirst
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-idempotency-0002

{
  "shippingAddress": { "recipientName": "Cara Customer", "line1": "42 Marine Drive",
                       "city": "Mumbai", "zone": "WEST", "postalCode": "400020", "phone": "9000000002" },
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentToken": "tok_success"
}

### B3. Send the IDENTICAL request again
# Same order id, same 201, header `Idempotent-Replay: true`, and ONE charge.
# No second order, no second unit of stock consumed.
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-idempotency-0002

{
  "shippingAddress": { "recipientName": "Cara Customer", "line1": "42 Marine Drive",
                       "city": "Mumbai", "zone": "WEST", "postalCode": "400020", "phone": "9000000002" },
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentToken": "tok_success"
}

### B4. Same key, DIFFERENT body -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED
# Replaying here would hand back an answer to a question nobody asked.
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-idempotency-0002

{
  "shippingAddress": { "recipientName": "Someone Else", "line1": "1 Other Road",
                       "city": "Delhi", "zone": "NORTH", "postalCode": "110001", "phone": "9000000005" },
  "paymentMethod": "UPI",
  "paymentToken": "tok_success",
  "couponCode": "SAVE10"
}

### B5. No key at all -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shippingAddress": { "recipientName": "Cara", "line1": "42 Marine Drive",
                       "city": "Mumbai", "zone": "WEST", "postalCode": "400020", "phone": "9000000002" },
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentToken": "tok_success"
}

###############################################################################
# SCENARIO C — payment failures
###############################################################################

### C1. Add an item
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 5, "quantity": 1 }

### C2. DECLINED -> 402. Stock released, order kept as PAYMENT_FAILED.
# A decline is final, so the hold goes straight back. The order is kept rather
# than deleted so the customer sees the attempt in their history.
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-decline-0003

{
  "shippingAddress": { "recipientName": "Cara", "line1": "42 Marine Drive",
                       "city": "Mumbai", "zone": "WEST", "postalCode": "400020", "phone": "9000000002" },
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentToken": "tok_decline"
}

### C3. Retry with the SAME key after the decline -> allowed, and succeeds
# A failed attempt releases the claim, so a transient decline does not lock the
# customer out permanently.
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-decline-0003

{
  "shippingAddress": { "recipientName": "Cara", "line1": "42 Marine Drive",
                       "city": "Mumbai", "zone": "WEST", "postalCode": "400020", "phone": "9000000002" },
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentToken": "tok_success"
}

### C4. Add another item for the timeout case
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 6, "quantity": 1 }

### C5. UNKNOWN OUTCOME -> 502, with `retrySafe: true`
# The hold is deliberately RETAINED: the charge may have succeeded, and releasing
# could sell units the customer already paid for. Payment -> UNCONFIRMED,
# order stays AWAITING_PAYMENT.
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-timeout-0004

{
  "shippingAddress": { "recipientName": "Cara", "line1": "42 Marine Drive",
                       "city": "Mumbai", "zone": "WEST", "postalCode": "400020", "phone": "9000000002" },
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentToken": "tok_timeout"
}

### C6. Log in as admin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@oms.dev", "password": "Password@123" }

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.data.accessToken); %}

### C7. The reconciliation queue — the UNCONFIRMED payment is visible, not buried
GET {{api}}/admin/payments/unconfirmed
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### C8. Orders still awaiting payment
# The default reservation TTL is 15 minutes. Wait it out (or shorten
# oms.inventory.reservation-ttl) and this order self-heals: the sweeper returns
# the stock and cancels the order. PaymentFailureIT proves this automatically.
GET {{api}}/admin/orders?status=AWAITING_PAYMENT
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###############################################################################
# SCENARIO D — oversell prevention
###############################################################################

### D1. Variant 9 (TEE-BLK-M) is seeded with exactly ONE unit network-wide
# 1 at Mumbai, 0 at Delhi. `available` is always derived as on_hand - reserved.
GET {{api}}/inventory/variants/9
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### D2. Ask for 3 of the 1 available -> 409 with a per-SKU shortfall breakdown
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 9, "quantity": 3 }

### D3. Attempt checkout
# Expect 409 INSUFFICIENT_STOCK with details: sku / requested / available.
# Nothing is held — TX-1 rolled back entirely.
POST {{api}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-oversell-0005

{
  "shippingAddress": { "recipientName": "Cara", "line1": "42 Marine Drive",
                       "city": "Mumbai", "zone": "WEST", "postalCode": "400020", "phone": "9000000002" },
  "paymentMethod": "CARD",
  "paymentToken": "tok_success"
}

### D4. Availability unchanged — a failed checkout leaks nothing
GET {{api}}/inventory/variants/9
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### D5. Tidy up
DELETE {{api}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

# For the real proof, 50 simultaneous checkouts against this one unit:
#   mvn verify -Dit.test=OversellPreventionIT -Dtest=MoneyTest

###############################################################################
# SCENARIO E — admin
###############################################################################

### E1. Category tree
GET {{api}}/categories

### E2. Create a category
POST {{api}}/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Wearables", "slug": "wearables", "parentId": 1 }

### E3. Create a product with a variant
POST {{api}}/admin/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Aurora Watch SE",
  "description": "1.8-inch AMOLED, 14-day battery.",
  "brand": "Aurora",
  "categoryId": 1,
  "variants": [
    { "sku": "AUR-WATCH-SE-BLK", "variantName": "Black", "price": 12999.00, "weightGrams": 48 }
  ]
}

### E4. Stock rows across warehouses
GET {{api}}/inventory?variantId=4
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### E5. Set an absolute level (stock-take)
# Refused with 422 if below units already reserved for open orders.
PUT {{api}}/admin/inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 4, "warehouseId": 1, "onHand": 40, "reorderLevel": 10, "reference": "STOCKTAKE-2026-09" }

### E6. Relative correction — safe to apply concurrently, unlike an absolute set
POST {{api}}/admin/inventory/adjustments
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 4, "warehouseId": 1, "quantityDelta": 12, "reference": "GRN-4471",
  "note": "Supplier delivery received" }

### E7. Movement ledger for one stock row (inventory item 8 = variant 4 @ WH-MUM)
GET {{api}}/inventory/8/ledger
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### E8. Low-stock report
GET {{api}}/inventory/low-stock
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### E9. Coupons with their redemption counters
GET {{api}}/admin/discounts
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### E10. Create a coupon
POST {{api}}/admin/discounts
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "WELCOME15",
  "description": "15% off your first order, capped at Rs.750",
  "type": "PERCENTAGE_OFF",
  "discountValue": 15.0,
  "maxDiscount": 750.00,
  "minOrderValue": 999.00,
  "startsAt": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "endsAt": "2027-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "usageLimit": 1000,
  "perCustomerLimit": 1
}

### E11. Tax rates — sparse by design; gaps inherit from an ancestor
GET {{api}}/admin/tax-rates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### E12. Set a rate. `rate` is a FRACTION: 0.28 means 28%.
PUT {{api}}/admin/tax-rates
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "categoryId": 2, "rate": 0.28, "description": "GST 28% — Mobiles" }

### E13. Outbox health. A non-zero deadLetter count needs a human.
GET {{api}}/admin/outbox/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### E14. Dead letters, with attempts and lastError
GET {{api}}/admin/outbox/dead-letters
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### E15. Full audit history for the order from Scenario A
# Every row carries the traceId of the request that caused it — including rows
# written asynchronously minutes later.
GET {{api}}/admin/audit-events/Order/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### E16. All orders
GET {{api}}/admin/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###############################################################################
# SCENARIO F — access control
###############################################################################

### F1. Customer hitting an admin endpoint -> 403
GET {{api}}/admin/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### F2. Staff trying to shop -> 403
GET {{api}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### F3. Staff CAN read stock (needed to pick), but cannot write it
GET {{api}}/inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### F4. Staff writing stock -> 403
PUT {{api}}/admin/inventory
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 4, "warehouseId": 1, "onHand": 9999 }

### F5. No token -> 401, in the same error shape as everything else
GET {{api}}/orders

### F6. Another customer cannot see this order -> 404, NOT 403
# A 403 would confirm the id exists and allow enumeration.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "customer2@oms.dev", "password": "Password@123" }

> {% client.global.set("otherCustomerToken", response.body.data.accessToken); %}

### F7. The attempt
GET {{api}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{otherCustomerToken}}

### F8. Validation errors are per-field in the standard envelope
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "not-an-email", "password": "short", "fullName": "" }

### F9. An expired coupon returns 422 with the reason, not a silent no-op
POST {{api}}/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "variantId": 4, "quantity": 1 }

### F10. Try it
POST {{api}}/cart/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "couponCode": "EXPIRED5" }
